omain — agree bit-for-bit** (2.9 s, 16 threads). This is a total equivalence proof, not a sample.\n\nTwo findings worth calling out, both in my tests rather than the translation:\n- My `nm --undefined-only` allowlist rejected `lseek64@GLIBC_2.2.5`/`realpath@GLIBC_2.3` — I was comparing versioned names; now stripped at `@`.\n- My structural guard flagged `if` as \"present in the C source\" because it's a substring of `m__shift`; now tokenised on identifier boundaries.\n\n**Negative control** (the part that makes the green result meaningful): I injected a 1-bit error affecting only `j=300` — a single index buried inside row 44's 103-wide run — and confirmed 7 tests across 3 suites caught it with exact diagnostics (`bits=0x96000000, C=0x8000 Rust=0x8001`). Notably `config_rows_all_86_base_shift_classes` **passed** through the injected bug, because it only samples each run's endpoints and midpoint; the randomized, all-512-`j`, and exhaustive tests are what caught it. That is direct evidence the layered coverage is doing real work rather than the suite being vacuously green. Source restored and re-verified afterward.\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`**, so there is exactly one configuration — `default` ≡ `--no-default-features`. `verify_all.sh` derives the power set from `Cargo.toml` programmatically (so it stays correct if features are ever added) and runs `cargo check --all-targets` plus the full suite in **both debug and release** for each combination, then asserts the `nm -D` diff is empty. Final run: `ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED`.\n\nCompletion gate: symbol diff empty ✅ · all 86 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass under randomized inputs ✅ · all 11 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing tests ✅ · holds under every feature combination and both profiles ✅. `c_src/` was not modified (only the out-of-tree `c_src/build/` the task's own instructions call for)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creat